Symbols: B=4 sequences, T=16 positions, C=128 channels, nh=4 heads, hs=32 head size, V=65 characters, L=4 blocks

== Forward pass (attention tensors shown for block 0; blocks 1..L-1 are the same) ==
| tensor | shape | what each dimension means |
|---|---|---|
| idx | (4, 16) | B sequences x T token positions; each entry is a character id in [0, V) |
| y (targets) | (4, 16) | B x T: the correct next character id for each position (x moved one place right) |
| tok_emb | (4, 16, 128) | B x T x C: one C-number embedding vector for each token |
| pos_emb | (16, 128) | T x C: one C-number vector for each position; it is added to every sequence (broadcast over B) |
| x0 = tok_emb + pos_emb | (4, 16, 128) | B x T x C: the residual stream that enters block 0 |
| attn.q | (4, 4, 16, 32) | B x nh x T x hs: the query of each head, for each position (C = nh x hs) |
| attn.k | (4, 4, 16, 32) | B x nh x T x hs: the key of each head, for each position |
| attn.v | (4, 4, 16, 32) | B x nh x T x hs: the value of each head, for each position |
| attn.scores (inside SDPA, not stored) | (4, 4, 16, 16) | B x nh x T x T: how much position t (row) looks at position s (column); causal, so s <= t |
| attn.y_heads | (4, 4, 16, 32) | B x nh x T x hs: the attention output of each head |
| attn.y_merged | (4, 16, 128) | B x T x C: the nh head outputs put side by side again |
| block[0] out | (4, 16, 128) | B x T x C: the residual stream after this block (attention + MLP, each with a residual add) |
| block[1] out | (4, 16, 128) | B x T x C: the residual stream after this block (attention + MLP, each with a residual add) |
| block[2] out | (4, 16, 128) | B x T x C: the residual stream after this block (attention + MLP, each with a residual add) |
| block[3] out | (4, 16, 128) | B x T x C: the residual stream after this block (attention + MLP, each with a residual add) |
| ln_f out | (4, 16, 128) | B x T x C: the residual stream after the last LayerNorm |
| logits | (4, 16, 65) | B x T x V: one score per vocabulary entry, for the next token at each position |
| loss | () | a scalar (shape ()): the mean cross-entropy over all B x T predictions |

